+## Optional v3 prefill ranks
+
+`prefill-ranks` invokes native `qwen-layer-stage-prefill-rank-check`. Its first
+public scope is exactly 65 prompt IDs, chunk 32, output one, no teacher,
+repeat one and zero warmups. It inherits the dense-Qwen artifact/loader limits
+above. The broader native 128/32 admission does not extend this launcher scope.
+It uses two local processes with an explicit fresh loopback epoch; SSH, JACCL,
+resident workers and multi-request serving are not exposed.
+
+```sh
+python3 experiments/cluster/run_stage_checks.py prefill-ranks \
+  --release RELEASE --runtime experiments/cluster/runtime --output NEW_OUTPUT \
+  --expected-binary-sha256 BINARY_SHA256 \
+  --model-dir LOCAL_MODEL --artifact-aggregate-sha256 ARTIFACT_SHA256 \
+  --tokens-file PROMPT_65_IDS_JSON --tokens-sha256 PROMPT_FILE_SHA256 \
+  --stage-prefill-policy serial_v1 --stage-logits-dtype bfloat16 \
+  --baseline-jsonl INDEPENDENT_NATIVE_BASELINE_JSONL \
+  --baseline-sha256 BASELINE_FILE_SHA256 \
+  --baseline-evidence-sha256 NATIVE_BASELINE_FINGERPRINT \
+  --timeout-seconds 180
+```
+
+`--stage-prefill-policy` is required: `serial_v1` or
+`prompt_lookahead_one_v1`. `--stage-logits-dtype` is also required:
+`float16`, `bfloat16`, or `float32`. The example dtype is not a default or a
+claim that all admitted artifacts have BF16 output. Admission reconstructs the
+saved baseline's native final-row bytes and requires its actual dtype to match.
+The source embedding activation dtype is independently taken from that same
+baseline's source identity; it is not inferred from the logits dtype.
+
+Both baseline pins are mandatory. `--baseline-sha256` hashes the exact JSONL
+file; `--baseline-evidence-sha256` pins the native `baseline.fingerprint`.
+The latter is recomputed from source identity, request fingerprint and all
+three frame/state/logit metadata fingerprints. The baseline must bind an
+independent request UUID with the identical 65 IDs and 32/32/1 schedule, the
+same artifact/configuration/plan and enabled source BF16 conversion policy.
+Its final vocabulary row and native dtype must be present. This checks supplied
+evidence integrity; it does not recreate that historical run or reverify its
+build, execution or model quality. Retain its original provenance and audit.
+
+Only this new command adds an initial **6 GiB actual-free** screen before
+source/bundle snapshots and artifact hashing. It records raw `vm_stat` and UTC.
+File caching during hashing can reduce actual free memory, so the screen does
+not promise 6 GiB remains at launch. The post-hash gate remains **8 GiB
+estimated reclaimable**, output storage and descriptor headroom. Memory
+pressure and zero-new-reported-swap are checked from before hashing through
+postflight. None of these screens guarantees whole-process memory usage.
+
+The v3 validator requires matching ready/final records, a closed version-three
+agreement with exact policy/dtypes/source/request bindings, equal peer
+agreements, verified source receipt identities, completed request retirement
+and released models. It retains the bounded native `execution` payload
+without interpreting its action trace, frame envelopes, selected token,
+final logit/state observations or timing arithmetic. Those require a separate
+independent audit. `baseline_admission` and outer validation can pass while
+`baseline_audit.performed` and `independent_numerical_action_timing_audit.performed`
+remain false. A launcher exit zero is not a numerical, throughput or physical
+transfer qualification. Existing P2P and v1 `ranks` validators are unchanged.
+
